    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d63">

                <pb facs="0082" n="73" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg73"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/521: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Oslo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-04-15">April 15,
                        1940</date>.<lb/>[Received April 15—7:31 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. From Cox.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d63-f1"/> Department’s 28, received 13.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>Estimated about 30.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d63-f2"/>
                    </item>
                    <label>(3)</label>
                    <item>Evacuation American citizens dependent reopening railroad connections with
                        Sweden, no communication whatever at present with Bergen and other Norwegian
                        centers. In view of above no definite plan can be formulated.</item>
                    <label>(4)</label>
                    <item>Cooperation Berlin authorities essential.</item>
                    <label>(5)</label>
                    <item>Estimate approximately 225 requiring all or part transportation expenses
                        particularly during present banking restrictions limiting withdrawals 500
                        crowns weekly 20,000 dollars.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d63-f1" n="10" xml:id="d63-f1-content">
                <p>Raymond E. Cox, First Secretary of Legation in Norway. Cox was signing for the
                    Ambassador, Mrs. Florence J. Harriman, who after the German invasion of Norway
                    entered Sweden on April 10, 1940.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d63-f2" n="11" xml:id="d63-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 291, May 6, the Chargé in Norway informed the Department that
                    this estimate was 300, not 30, but had then been reduced to 250
                    (340.1115A/579).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
